## 5 non-negotiable rules

### 1 — `packages/core/src/v3/` has zero infrastructure imports

No `drizzle-orm`, `postgres`, `pg`, `ioredis`, `redis`, or `@neondatabase` inside `packages/core/src/v3/`. Enforced by vitest purity tests (NOT lint):
- `packages/types/src/__tests__/purity.test.ts`
- `packages/core/src/__tests__/v3-purity.test.ts`

Run: `pnpm --filter @mnemosyne/core test`

### 2 — All `mnemo_*` queries MUST go through `withMnemoTx(workspaceId, fn)`

Bypassing it silently disables RLS → cross-workspace data leak. Source: `packages/core/src/tx.ts`

### 3 — Sensitivity comparison uses `SENSITIVITY_ORDER` numeric map — NEVER string equality (MED-23)

`"confidential" > "internal"` is alphabetically true but semantically wrong. Always use `SENSITIVITY_ORDER[tier]` from `packages/types/src/security.ts`.

### 4 — Sensitivity ceiling violations return 404, not 403

404 prevents an attacker from confirming that the resource exists (anti-probing).

### 5 — The 9 relation verbs are locked

```
related | compatible | scoped | conflicts_with | supersedes
not_conflict | derived_from | part_of | member_of
```

SQL CHECK constraint in `packages/adapter-postgres/migrations/v3/0001_baseline.sql` enforces this. Do not invent new verbs.

### 6 — Bitemporal model: `validFrom/validTo` ≠ `createdAt`

`validFrom/validTo` = when the fact was **true in the world** (domain time — used by `?asOf=` queries and recall).
`createdAt` = when Mnemosyne **recorded** it (system time).

A decision made last year but recorded today: `validFrom: <last year>`, `createdAt: <today>`. Never store discovery time in `validFrom`, and never use `createdAt` for time-travel queries.

